  "title": "DTLS: Scan server hello correctly",
  "description": "When calling tls_scan_server_hello, the entire record length includes\nthe 12 octet offset for the start of the handshake, so too large an\nend offset was passed into tls_scan_server_hello, possibly leading\nto exceptions on the first pass for DTLS 1.2 (running off the end\nof the handshake message looking for the extension.)\n\nAlso guard against the ServerHello being fragmented for some reason.\n\nFix up 9710a98b67c5013b0eb4a0583f9e2326b8a6ddab",
